INSERT INTO google_book values ("Yp56DQAAQBAJ", "I Tied My Shoes Today", '{"kind":"books#volume","id":"Yp56DQAAQBAJ","etag":"ioE65Ec4xoQ","selfLink":"https://www.googleapis.com/books/v1/volumes/Yp56DQAAQBAJ","volumeInfo":{"title":"I Tied My Shoes Today","subtitle":"Recovering from a Hemorrhagic Stroke","authors":["Megon Phillips Aesch"],"publisher":"Archway Publishing","publishedDate":"2016-11-08","description":"Author Megon Phillips Aesch was a thirty-four-year-old, career-oriented horticulturist with a good business and a great husband. They had dreams, goals, and focus. They had a plan, and then disaster struck, hit with a blow beyond imagination. Megon suffered a stroke caused by an arteriovenous malformation (AVM). It transformed her from a strong-willed, independent business woman to a patient in a wheelchair requiring a great deal of assistance. In I Tied My Shoes Today, Megon shares her story in conjunction with her husband, Jim, who kept a journal while she was incapacitated and recovering from the stroke. It tells how she and her family faced the challenges of a traumatic injury to her brainthe setbacks, the triumphs, and the life-and-death decisions that were encountered for almost two years. A story about love, growth, disaster, and renewal, I Tied My Shoes Today narrates the gamut of emotions and events in Megons pursuit to return to her former self. It also tells about the symptoms and causes of stroke and describes the practices and the policies the medical profession follows.","industryIdentifiers":[{"type":"ISBN_13","identifier":"9781480836556"},{"type":"ISBN_10","identifier":"1480836559"}],"readingModes":{"text":true,"image":true},"pageCount":121,"printType":"BOOK","categories":["Self-Help"],"maturityRating":"NOT_MATURE","allowAnonLogging":false,"contentVersion":"1.2.3.0.preview.3","panelizationSummary":{"containsEpubBubbles":false,"containsImageBubbles":false},"imageLinks":{"smallThumbnail":"http://books.google.com/books/content?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=5&edge=curl&source=gbs_api","thumbnail":"http://books.google.com/books/content?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=1&edge=curl&source=gbs_api"},"language":"en","previewLink":"http://books.google.co.jp/books?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ&pg=PT70&dq=i&hl=&cd=2&source=gbs_api","infoLink":"https://play.google.com/store/books/details?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ&source=gbs_api","canonicalVolumeLink":"https://play.google.com/store/books/details?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ"},"saleInfo":{"country":"JP","saleability":"FOR_SALE","isEbook":true,"listPrice":{"amount":550,"currencyCode":"JPY"},"retailPrice":{"amount":495,"currencyCode":"JPY"},"buyLink":"https://play.google.com/store/books/details?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ&rdid=book-Yp56DQAAQBAJ&rdot=1&source=gbs_api","offers":[{"finskyOfferType":1,"listPrice":{"amountInMicros":550000000,"currencyCode":"JPY"},"retailPrice":{"amountInMicros":495000000,"currencyCode":"JPY"}}]},"accessInfo":{"country":"JP","viewability":"PARTIAL","embeddable":true,"publicDomain":false,"textToSpeechPermission":"ALLOWED","epub":{"isAvailable":true,"acsTokenLink":"http://books.google.co.jp/books/download/I_Tied_My_Shoes_Today-sample-epub.acsm?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ&format=epub&output=acs4_fulfillment_token&dl_type=sample&source=gbs_api"},"pdf":{"isAvailable":true,"acsTokenLink":"http://books.google.co.jp/books/download/I_Tied_My_Shoes_Today-sample-pdf.acsm?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ&format=pdf&output=acs4_fulfillment_token&dl_type=sample&source=gbs_api"},"webReaderLink":"http://play.google.com/books/reader?id=Yp56DQAAQBAJ&hl=&source=gbs_api","accessViewStatus":"SAMPLE","quoteSharingAllowed":false},"searchInfo":{"textSnippet":"... <b>I</b> asked if we were going right home , or if we had to stop someplace on the way home . The reason for this was so that <b>I</b> could figure out where the nearest bathroom was and how it was set up in case <b>I</b> needed one . Was <b>I</b> familiar with it&nbsp;..."}}');
INSERT INTO google_book values ("x-zxCAAAQBAJ", "Part I: Physical Chemistry. Part II: Solid State Physics", '{"kind":"books#volume","id":"x-zxCAAAQBAJ","etag":"HEj92SGVsuo","selfLink":"https://www.googleapis.com/books/v1/volumes/x-zxCAAAQBAJ","volumeInfo":{"title":"Part I: Physical Chemistry. Part II: Solid State Physics","authors":["Arthur S. Wightman"],"publisher":"Springer","publishedDate":"2013-12-11","description":"The fourth volume of the Collected Works is devoted to Wigner''s contribution to physical chemistry, statistical mechanics and solid-state physics. In his annotation to the first part, N. Balazs clearly points out Wigner''s role in early quantum chemistry and applied statistical mechanics. One corner stone was his introducing of what is now called the Wigner function, and his paper on adiabatic perturbations foreshadowed later work on Berry phases. Although few in number, Wigner''s articles on solid-state physics laid the ground for the modern theory of the electronic structure of metals. W. Kohn writes about this in his annotation to Part 2 of the book and he also points out Wigner''s great influence in the development of solid-state theory.","industryIdentifiers":[{"type":"ISBN_13","identifier":"9783642590337"},{"type":"ISBN_10","identifier":"3642590330"}],"readingModes":{"text":false,"image":true},"pageCount":463,"printType":"BOOK","categories":["Science"],"maturityRating":"NOT_MATURE","allowAnonLogging":false,"contentVersion":"0.2.1.0.preview.1","panelizationSummary":{"containsEpubBubbles":false,"containsImageBubbles":false},"imageLinks":{"smallThumbnail":"http://books.google.com/books/content?id=x-zxCAAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=5&edge=curl&source=gbs_api","thumbnail":"http://books.google.com/books/content?id=x-zxCAAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=1&edge=curl&source=gbs_api"},"language":"en","previewLink":"http://books.google.co.jp/books?id=x-zxCAAAQBAJ&pg=PA220&dq=i&hl=&cd=3&source=gbs_api","infoLink":"https://play.google.com/sto